# Day 17: Persisting Configuration

## Phase 4 - Environment, Vim & Text Processing | Day 17 of 30

## Commands covered today
See commands.md for all 10 commands with syntax and my own explanation
of what each one does and when I would reach for it.

## What I practiced
I added a permanent environment variable and a custom alias to my
.bashrc, reloaded it with source instead of opening a new terminal, and
confirmed both persisted in a fresh session afterward.

## What surprised me
Yesterday I learned export only lasts for the current session — today
made that click fully. Putting the same export line inside .bashrc is
what actually makes it permanent, since .bashrc runs automatically
every time a new shell starts. The variable itself doesn't change; it's
just where you define it that determines whether it survives.

